592186117563 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186117567 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117563 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186117568 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117563 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117563 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117563 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "de75ec3a-0ae7-5e53-b679-aa489a6e2938" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117564 #edb/ref 1080 "r = ⟨0, 2,-0.5⟩ + s⟨1, 3, 0⟩ + t⟨1,-1, 3⟩, s, t ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117564 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117564 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "941f6bb6-ca0b-5ea1-b87c-af2fa80d4876" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117565 #edb/ref 1080 "None of the listed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117565 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117565 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "986efc18-be18-5b16-b8b4-99fc183d1672" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117566 #edb/ref 1080 "r = ⟨1,-1, 3⟩ + s⟨1, 3, 0⟩ + t⟨0, 2,-0.5⟩, s, t ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117566 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117566 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1395bc4f-e4f7-5963-be28-263b9823d510" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117567 #edb/ref 1080 "r = s⟨1, 3, 0⟩ + t⟨0, 2,-0.5⟩, s, t ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117567 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117567 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5fdc530d-3b00-5f5d-8bc0-018659ce8625" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117568 #edb/ref 1080 "r = ⟨1, 3, 0⟩ + s⟨1,-1, 3⟩ + t⟨0, 2,-0.5⟩, s, t ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117568 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117568 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "643bbf8e-a5ac-5da5-8c23-895f54546f79" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119647 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4940" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119647 #edb/ref 1071 "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(-3,2,5)$ and is parallel to the vectors $\\mathbf{b}= \\langle 17,3,15 \\rangle$  and $\\mathbf{c}= \\langle 5,0,-8 \\rangle.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119647 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a6fded96-287a-53ee-8b1c-dd618562b2c2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119647 #edb/ref 1074 "A parametric equation of a plane is given by \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}=\\mathbf{p}+ s\\mathbf{b}+ t \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{p}$ is the position vector of a point on the plane and the vectors $\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\mathbf{c}$ are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nHere, the position vector of the given point $P$ is $\\mathbf{p}=\\langle -3,2,5 \\rangle,$ and the two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other) are $\\mathbf{b}= \\langle 17,3,15 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{c}= \\langle 5,0,-8 \\rangle.$\n\nSo, a parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨-3,2,5⟩+s\\,⟨17,3,15⟩+t\\,⟨5,0,-8⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119648 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4941" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119648 #edb/ref 1071 "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $C(2,50,-19)$ and is parallel to the lines $\\mathbf{r}= \\langle 2,\\sqrt{6},17 \\rangle + s \\langle -1,7,2 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{r}= \\langle 20,-44, 27 \\rangle + t \\langle 2\\sqrt{3},9,-8 \\rangle$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119648 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "297bda8f-6e33-5cc2-a2e1-5ab6186fa9d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119648 #edb/ref 1074 "The direction vectors of the lines are $\\mathbf{v_1}=\\langle  -1,7,2  \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{v_2}=\\langle 2\\sqrt{3},9,-8 \\rangle$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $C(2,50,-19)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle 2,50,-19 \\rangle.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =c+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨2,50,-19⟩+s\\,⟨-1,7,2⟩+t\\,⟨2\\sqrt{3},9,-8⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119649 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4942" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119649 #edb/ref 1071 "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $A(-1,4,-3),$ $B(7,5,4),$ and $C(2,-2,8).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119649 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9c36ddd5-fcf1-5c4d-a350-aa8ef3a3ca9e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119649 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨7,5,4⟩-⟨-1,4,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8,1,7⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =⟨2,-2,8⟩-⟨-1,4,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-6,11⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle -1,4,-3 \\rangle$ of the point $A,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =a+s\\overset{\\to }{AB}+t\\overset{\\to }{AC} \\\\ r & =⟨-1,4,-3⟩+s⟨8,1,7⟩+t⟨3,-6,11⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Watch out!** The form of the final equation depends on our choice of vectors and the point on the plane. We could have picked other vectors. Likewise, we could have chosen $B$ or $C$ instead of $A$ as our point on the plane. So, the answer is *not unique*!" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119664 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5884" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119664 #edb/ref 1071 "Find a normal vector to the plane \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}= \\langle -6,3, 2 \\rangle + t \\langle 4, 2, -1 \\rangle + s \\langle 4, -3, 2 \\rangle,\\qquad t,\\,s \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119664 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b86eace4-01cb-5601-8e9b-2658e81fc656" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119664 #edb/ref 1074 "From the parametric equation, we have that $\\mathbf{v} = \\langle 4, 2, -1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{w} = \\langle 4, -3, 2 \\rangle$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $\\mathbf{v}$ and $\\mathbf{w}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =i-12j-20k \\\\  & =⟨1,-12,-20⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $\\mathbf{n}=\\langle 1, -12, -20 \\rangle.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119933 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119933 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186120234 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119933 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186120235 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119933 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186262902 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119933 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186262903 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119933 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186262904 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119933 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186304903 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119933 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186338858 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119933 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186338859 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119933 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186338860 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119933 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186338861 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119933 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Parallel To Two Given Vectors" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119933 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186119647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119933 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "b02f02f1-f270-55e0-a7a9-0b729c4d82c0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119934 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049132 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119934 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186120277 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119934 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186120278 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119934 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186262915 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119934 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186262916 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119934 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186311921 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119934 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186311922 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119934 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186311923 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119934 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186338862 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119934 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186338863 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119934 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186391682 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119934 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding a Normal Vector To a Plane Given by Parametric Equation" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119934 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186119664 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119934 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "62196ae9-df2e-5a3a-bc0a-1c0f4c40af3e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119935 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186120225 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119935 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186120236 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119935 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186262922 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119935 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186338864 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119935 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186338865 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119935 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186338866 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119935 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186364961 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119935 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186387887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119935 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186393057 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119935 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186398347 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119935 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Parallel To Two Lines" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119935 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186119648 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119935 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "3061cb06-f57f-57c8-8821-dbd962b1e78e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119936 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186120218 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119936 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186120219 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119936 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186262927 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119936 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186262928 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119936 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186262929 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119936 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186304926 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119936 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186338879 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119936 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186338881 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119936 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186366205 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119936 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186387957 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119936 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186387964 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119936 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186393064 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119936 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Passing Through Three Given Points" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119936 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186119649 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119936 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "d11f13f0-1cfa-59ec-a04a-9483d942b1aa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120017 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186120897 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120017 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186120898 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120017 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186120899 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120017 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186120900 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120017 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186120901 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120017 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186120902 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120017 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120017 #edb/ref 1045 "The Parametric Equations of a Plane" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120017 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186120897 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120017 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050308 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120017 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "4a64e93c-7c38-5a2c-bcd0-c1efea32558e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120234 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186117563 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120234 #edb/ref 1069 "q-33154" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120234 #edb/ref 1071 "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(1,-1, 3)$ and is parallel to the vectors $v_{1} = ⟨1, 3, 0⟩$ and $v_{2} = ⟨0, 2,-0.5⟩$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120234 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "001b7edd-c428-5436-8d89-3502541770a4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120236 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304576 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120236 #edb/ref 1069 "q-33158" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120236 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120236 #edb/ref 1071 "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $B(-2,23,14)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨-3,5,1⟩+s⟨-3,5,4⟩$ and $r=⟨-30,55,25⟩+t⟨4,7,-1⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120236 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "88872368-686b-5e7f-9016-e33ff5ee0ad5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120236 #edb/ref 1074 "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨-3,5,4⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨4,7,-1⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $B(-2,23,14)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $b=⟨-2,23,14⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =b+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨-2,23,14⟩+s⟨-3,5,4⟩+t⟨4,7,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120278 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186310841 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120278 #edb/ref 1069 "q-33818" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120278 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120278 #edb/ref 1071 "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=⟨2,0,-1⟩+t⟨-2,-7,5⟩+s⟨2,12,5⟩,\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120278 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "183d75ab-bc55-5284-9356-4879f8cd6310" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120278 #edb/ref 1074 "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-2,-7,5⟩$ and $w=⟨2,12,5⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -2 & -7 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 12 & 5\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-95i+20j-10k \\\\  & =⟨-95,20,-10⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-95,20,-10⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120897 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120898 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120897 #edb/ref 1061 421992 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120897 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9e58d46a-ae91-5ee2-88e7-83dddd91cd81" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120897 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186121051 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120898 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120899 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120898 #edb/ref 1061 421993 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120898 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9f747cb6-7704-53df-bc68-9a201f538aa3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120898 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119933 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120899 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120900 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120899 #edb/ref 1061 421996 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120899 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "aa340a23-a5f7-53c0-a279-cfaa2cb34f68" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120899 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119934 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120900 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120901 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120900 #edb/ref 1061 421999 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120900 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0b7d4f28-8841-5518-ad36-74e1aa0d9163" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120900 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119935 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120901 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120902 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120901 #edb/ref 1061 422002 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120901 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "43769a60-5b42-5a2c-82fa-0054a159b437" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120901 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186121052 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120902 #edb/ref 1061 422003 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120902 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a2d3f79a-dc28-5d90-9d1f-404334ec9529" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120902 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119936 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121051 #edb/ref 1064 "Any plane can be uniquely determined by a point and two non-parallel direction vectors. For example, let $\\Pi$ be the plane that passes through the point $P(1,0,2)$ and is parallel to the vectors $\\mathbf{b}= \\langle 0,3,0 \\rangle$  and $\\mathbf{c}= \\langle -1,1,1 \\rangle.$\n\n![](images/ea/ea4ce822abec2b68d2471a2787f4e045493ca43c1c6795a7e0069de80cb5adee.png)\n\nUsing the vectors $\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\mathbf{c},$ we can construct a **parametric equation** of the plane.\n\nFirst, let $R$ be any general point in the plane, with position vector $\\mathbf{r}.$ Notice that we can get from $P$ to $R$ using a linear combination of $\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\mathbf{c}$ with some (unknown for us) coefficients $s$ and $t$, as shown below.\n\n![](images/b4/b40f91c3d75f092c7b29f19770364e7518d37b64ba594a311a762ad79a950e4f.png)\n\nSo, we can write the **parametric equation** of the plane as\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}\\mathbf{r}} = \\mathbf{p}+s{\\color{blue}\\,\\mathbf{b}}+t\\,{\\color{blue}\\mathbf{c}},\n\t\\qquad s,t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).\n$$\n\nThis formula works whenever $\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\mathbf{c}$ are not parallel.\n\nIn our case, $\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\mathbf{c}$ are indeed not parallel to each other. So, using column vector notation, the parametric equation for the plane $\\Pi$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121051 #edb/ref 1065 3257 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121051 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "2828346e-3bca-51a8-a6ef-a86ca7034a62" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121051 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121052 #edb/ref 1064 "Any plane can be uniquely determined by three non-collinear points. \n\n![](images/08/08e65c4e3465a4bf155dfed6bc0dc2a35bf2eb9326d9bff0c0aa75b86e97d76b.png)\n\nTo write down a parametric equation of the plane, the trick is to use the three non-collinear points to construct two displacement vectors that are parallel to the plane.\n\n![](images/16/1613ea9df76b637b93e0e4b38b70b87892140398eaa7aaccb74f2a5642124dfd.png)\n\nThen we can proceed as usual to find the equation of the plane. Let's practice this technique in the following example." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121052 #edb/ref 1065 3258 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121052 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "e32f2dc4-38f6-541d-9dc6-9cfd1ac079eb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121052 #edb/ref 1067 "Finding the Equation of a Plane Passing Through Three Points" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186260257 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨6,-4,-26⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186260257 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186260257 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2b4a3c41-2d3e-5406-a2cd-cbab49cb529e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186260737 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨8,-2,17⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186260737 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186260737 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "63d710f5-99cb-53b4-8290-6299023ee722" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186261175 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨-8,-2,-22⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186261175 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186261175 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "95c11743-7580-55cc-a7f1-587f795b6ee6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186261244 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨-8,2,-11⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186261244 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186261244 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9e1ed729-7d24-5fef-a919-3b87d20a7b2c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186261803 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨-2,-8,-7⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186261803 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186261803 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "da606c57-af3e-52fa-9552-99fdba561ef0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262532 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186260257 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262532 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186260737 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262532 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186261175 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262532 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186261244 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262532 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186261803 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262532 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262532 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262532 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186261175 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262532 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e859b94c-82b3-57fc-b159-f1a0791b5216" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262916 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186262532 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262916 #edb/ref 1069 "q-128497" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262916 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262916 #edb/ref 1071 "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=⟨3,\\sqrt{7},-2⟩+t⟨-2,8,0⟩+s⟨3,-1,-1⟩,\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262916 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "58d7da64-39e5-5263-82e1-d46d43bc9c9d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262916 #edb/ref 1074 "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-2,8,0⟩$ and $w=⟨3,-1,-1⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -2 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-8i-2j-22k \\\\  & =⟨-8,-2,-22⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-8,-2,-22⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302705 #edb/ref 1080 "r=⟨-2,23,14⟩+s⟨-3,5,4⟩+t⟨4,7,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302705 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302705 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2646d87e-2e74-5757-bc34-02f20d6114fd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302774 #edb/ref 1080 "The plane is undefined" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302774 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302774 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "336bb496-d1df-5e9a-a07a-1ec951355ede" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303040 #edb/ref 1080 "r=⟨-2,23,14⟩+s⟨-3,5,1⟩+t⟨-30,55,25⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303040 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303040 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5ff6b838-1af4-5c00-868a-734468c82814" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303091 #edb/ref 1080 "The plane is undefined" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303091 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303091 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "68558628-ae8a-519a-9cf8-9a1b1e7f6286" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303341 #edb/ref 1080 "r=⟨-2,-2,-2⟩+s⟨1,4,-14⟩+t⟨1,1,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303341 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303341 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8e8dad69-2acf-5472-9a3f-505a95ac3fea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303557 #edb/ref 1080 "r=⟨1,4,-14⟩+s⟨-2,-2,-2⟩+t⟨1,1,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186303557 #edb/ref 1082