079 #uuid "3a308e92-1035-59ed-9244-1f44706e0efe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304576 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186302705 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304576 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186303040 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304576 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186303091 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304576 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186303676 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304576 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186303894 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304576 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304576 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304576 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186302705 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304576 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b8f249d4-cd35-55dd-9318-5acc4887eb5e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304926 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186304233 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304926 #edb/ref 1069 "q-33160" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304926 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304926 #edb/ref 1071 "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $C(1,4,-14)$ and is parallel to the two distinct lines $r=⟨-1,5,7⟩+s⟨1,1,1⟩$ and $r=⟨0,3,-19⟩+t⟨-2,-2,-2⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304926 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "133e1de3-de48-5298-8948-a57726f1d155" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186304926 #edb/ref 1074 "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨-2,-2,-2⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨1,1,1⟩,$ respectively.\nBut ${v}_{2}=-2{v}_{1}.$ So, our lines are parallel. \n\nDespite this fact, two distinct parallel lines still determine a plane. Now: \n\n- from the equation of the first line, we get the point $P$ with the position vector $p=⟨-1,5,7⟩$ that lies on it, and\n\n- from the equation of the second line, we get the point $Q$ with the position vector $q=⟨0,3,-19⟩$ that lies on it.\n\nThe vector $u=q-p$ will be parallel to the required plane. \n\nComputing the coordinates of $u,$  we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =q-p \\\\  & =⟨0,3,-19⟩-⟨-1,5,7⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-2,-26⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}∦{v}_{1},$ we can find the equation of our plane.\n\nWe know that the point $C(1,4,-14)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $c=⟨1,4,-14⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =c+s{v}_{1}+tu \\\\ r & =⟨1,4,-14⟩+s⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨1,-2,-26⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308877 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨-59,10,-20⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308877 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308877 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "11b5e92d-6224-56f5-944e-a8b83ad251a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186309632 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨-95,20,-10⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186309632 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186309632 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "719fd09d-d078-59ed-81b8-c5e456b9a391" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186309648 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨2,0,-1⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186309648 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186309648 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "740f86a3-b4cf-5219-84a0-d82570a20efd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186309908 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨-4,-84,25⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186309908 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186309908 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "90ffb081-cc79-57a0-a759-a970dcf68248" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186310170 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨-2,-7,5⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186310170 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186310170 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b018f396-0291-53b4-b697-3ecdf0cb89a7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186310841 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186308877 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186310841 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186309632 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186310841 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186309648 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186310841 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 